    "plan_strategy": "Single attempt: swap the linear baseline for a gradient-boosted tree ensemble (hist_gbdt) to lift the ranking itself, and move the operating point with an explicit mild class weight so the default 0.5 cut lands near the balanced-accuracy optimum. Concretely: hist_gbdt with learning_rate 0.06, max_iter 500, max_leaf_nodes 63, min_samples_leaf 20, l2_regularization 1.0, early_stopping enabled with validation_fraction 0.1 and n_iter_no_change 30 so capacity is set by the data rather than a guess. Preprocessing: impute 'none' so the tree splits on NaN in workclass/occupation/native-country itself (these are one-hot encoded levels plus 6 numeric columns; NaN handling costs nothing and no indicator columns are added, since they are provably redundant under impute:none), no scaling (trees are scale-invariant, and capital-gain/fnlwgt skew is irrelevant to split finding). class_weight is not a hist_gbdt parameter, so the operating point is moved via sample-free means only — instead I rely on the ranking gain plus the reported cut_headroom to tell the operator where the remaining gap is."
